      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Reject duplicate ranks while parsing tiktoken vocab files.\r\n- Add a regression test that loads two valid base64 tokens with rank `0` through `TiktokenTokenizer::new()`.\r\n\r\nFixes #50954\r\n\r\n## Reproduction and result\r\n\r\nBefore this change, the production fallback reached `tiktoken-rs::CoreBPE::new`, which panicked because encoder and decoder lengths differed for duplicate ranks.\r\n\r\nAfter this change, the shared tiktoken parsing boundary returns:\r\n\r\n```\r\ntokenizer error: duplicate rank 0 in tiktoken file\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe malformed input is therefore rejected before either tokenizer backend receives it. Sparse but unique ranks remain allowed.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- `cargo fmt --check`\r\n- `cargo test -p vllm-tokenizer` (63 passed; doc-tests passed)\r\n- `cargo clippy -p vllm-tokenizer --all-targets -- -D warnings`\r\n\r\n## AI assistance disclosure\r\n\r\nThis pull request was developed by using AI assistance. \r\n",
